From 40d1e3a36a4193e8d500af198bf1981143fb600c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nour <stefan.nour@adesso-romania.ro>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 07:45:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(serve): encrypt verdict text in serve.answer for
 encrypted runs (L5-F2)

Security-hardening mission 2026-09-01, task B21 (finding L5-F2, HIGH).
Handoff patch series for the live mission's orchestrator; NOT merged into
the security branch. Base: b5a6b6eb (origin/dev).

Encrypted runs persisted their final verdict / hypothesis / research-plan
text in plaintext in serve.answer.answer_form (packages/serve/src/index.ts:
the answerForm derivation, the serve.answer INSERT, the answer_form
projection read) because serve.answer was never declared in the 0038
carrier set. The AEAD control was bypassed for the highest-value derived
artifact.

Now, for a run with content_encryption_version=1, ServeRepository.persist
encrypts {answerForm} with the run content key through the existing
encryptAttestedContentForRun path (carrier "serve.answer", primary key
answer_id) before the write transaction, stores the JSON compatibility
sentinel in answer_form plus content_ciphertext / content_attestation, and
readAnswerProjection decrypts it beside core.run, serve.fact_bundle and
serve.composed_text. readReviewCatchUpSource (the runner's supersede path)
already reads through that projection. Legacy plaintext rows keep NULL
carrier columns, the existing legacy marking, and read exactly as before.

Migration migrations/0057_serve_answer_content_carrier.sql carries a
PROVISIONAL NUMBER: the live mission continues from 0057 after the security
mission's 0056, so the folding orchestrator must renumber it to the next
free slot (nothing inside it depends on the number; the tests locate it by
suffix). It adds the two carrier columns to serve.answer, re-declares
core.enforce_content_ciphertext() (0038 body verbatim plus one serve.answer
ELSIF) and core.enforce_content_attestation_v2() (0040 body verbatim plus
one CASE arm), and attaches the three carrier triggers (attestation,
plaintext-write guard, erasure barrier; the barrier function is unchanged
because its generic branch resolves run_id). Additive and replay-safe; no
historical tuple is rewritten.

Outside packages/serve, migrations and tests: packages/crypto/src/index.ts
gains "serve.answer" in CONTENT_CARRIERS (the ContentCarrier union derives
from it; nothing else can express a new carrier). packages/db is untouched.

RED first: tests/integration/serve-answer-content-encryption.test.ts on the
untouched base fails at the stored-row assertion, the verdict marker
appearing verbatim in SELECT to_jsonb(answer) FROM serve.answer. GREEN
after the change: 2/2 in 9.7 s on real embedded PostgreSQL (sentinel plus
envelope on the row, projection decrypts, a direct plaintext INSERT raises
CONTENT_PLAINTEXT_WRITE_FORBIDDEN: serve.answer, the legacy row is
unchanged, a run-key shred makes the envelope and the projection
unrecoverable while the legacy row stays readable, and the migration
replays cleanly). tests/architecture/s6-content-encryption-contract.test.ts
pins the new carrier (7/7). tests/unit/s6-content-encryption.test.ts is
15/16: the one failure (ZodError REGISTER_VERSION NaN at line 586) is
pre-existing and identical with this change stashed. Typecheck: only the
8 pre-existing tests/unit/s14-ui.test.ts errors.

Residual for the orchestrator: the envelope is bound to answer_id only,
because answer_version is allocated inside the write transaction after key
material must already be prepared, so two versions of one answer share an
attestation scope (every other carrier binds by its single uuid as well).

